---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
---

<SiteLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Pilly handles local medicine data, optional Pilly Plus accounts, purchases, and private photos.">
  <article class="legal shell">
    <header class="legal-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>Effective {site.legalEffectiveDate}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="legal-summary">
      <strong>The short version</strong>
      <p>
        Pilly works without an account. Medicine tracking stays on your device unless you sign in to
        Pilly Plus and explicitly turn on private backup. We do not sell your data or use it for ads.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section>
      <h2>What Pilly stores on your device</h2>
      <p>
        Pilly stores the information you enter—such as medicine names, schedules, dose records,
        supply estimates, appearance choices, profile details, and app settings—in local storage on
        your device. Local reminders are scheduled through the operating system. Pilly’s notification
        copy is designed not to reveal medicine names on the lock screen.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Optional Pilly Plus account and backup</h2>
      <p>
        If you choose Pilly Plus, Pilly uses Amazon Cognito to connect an Apple or Google account. We
        receive a stable account identifier and may receive your email address, relay email address,
        and display name from the provider. We use this information only to authenticate you,
        identify your Pilly account, provide support, and operate the features you request.
      </p>
      <p>
        Signing in alone does not upload your medicine data. If you explicitly enable private backup,
        Pilly synchronizes the medicine records needed for backup and recovery, including medicines,
        schedules, dose and supply history, and intentionally account-scoped profile data. Optional
        medicine photos and your optional account avatar are stored privately in Amazon S3.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Google user data</h2>
      <p>
        When you continue with Google, Pilly requests only basic OpenID identity information: your
        Google account identifier, email address, and profile information. Pilly uses this data to
        create and secure your optional Pilly Plus account. Pilly does not access Google Drive,
        contacts, calendars, health data, or other Google services, and does not use Google user data
        for advertising.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Purchases</h2>
      <p>
        Apple processes App Store purchases. RevenueCat helps Pilly validate purchases and determine
        whether Pilly Plus is active. Pilly sends RevenueCat a Pilly account identifier and purchase
        information needed to manage your entitlement. Medicine records and photos are not sent to
        RevenueCat.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Service providers</h2>
      <p>Pilly uses a small set of providers to deliver the features you choose:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Amazon Web Services for optional account authentication, private backup, and photo storage;</li>
        <li>Apple for Sign in with Apple, App Store purchases, notifications, and platform services;</li>
        <li>Google for optional Google sign-in; and</li>
        <li>RevenueCat for subscription status and purchase lifecycle management.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These providers process data under their own terms and privacy commitments. Information may
        be processed in locations outside your country where these providers operate.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Analytics, advertising, and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Pilly does not include third-party advertising or behavioral analytics. This website does not
        use analytics cookies, advertising cookies, account sign-in, or tracking pixels.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your choices and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        You can use the free tracker without creating an account. You can turn private backup on only
        when you choose it, remove individual photos, sign out, export a readable copy of local data,
        or delete your cloud account from within Pilly. Cloud account deletion removes synchronized
        account records and private images. Local information remains under your device controls
        until you delete it or remove the app.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Security and retention</h2>
      <p>
        Pilly uses authenticated, owner-scoped access for cloud records and private images. No system
        can guarantee absolute security. We retain optional cloud information while your Pilly Plus
        account exists and as reasonably necessary to provide the service, resolve security or
        support issues, and meet legal obligations. Deletion requests are processed through the app.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Pilly is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
        information from children under 13. A parent or guardian who believes a child has provided
        personal information can contact us to request deletion.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as Pilly changes. The effective date above will identify the latest
        version. Questions or privacy requests can be sent to
        <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
